    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "David Scally of David Ross Estate Agents, your local property experts are delighted to present new to market 136 Old County Road\r\nWe are extremely thrilled to present you with a unique opportunity to acquire this charming, original red brick home, with a large south facing garden, nestled away in this most sought after enclave.\r\nThe entire house is bathed in natural light, which adds to its inviting ambiance all whilst retaining a charming and characterful feel throughout. \r\nOn the ground floor it comprises an entrance hall, living room with feature fireplace to the front aspect and beyond is a second large reception /dining room and to complete the ground floor is a small fully fitted kitchen.\r\nOn the first floor you will find three generously sized bedrooms as well as a family bathroom.\r\nLocated just off the Crumlin Road Its location offers great convenience, providing quick and easy access to the city centre and an array of amenities just a stone's throw away. \r\nFrom retail to coffee shops, local independent convenience shops, numerous bus routes, parks, and an excellent selection of schools are all within close proximity. A ten-minute walk leads to the Luas red line, further enhancing accessibility. The Iveagh Grounds, a versatile sports facility, hosts clubs for Rugby, Hockey, GAA, and Soccer, while nearby Sundrive Park is home to running and tennis clubs, featuring a cycling track for enthusiasts. The Crumlin Children's Hospital is just a 5-minute walk away. The location is superb as it is close to Crumlin Village, Kimmage, Walkinstown and Terenure.\r\nViewing by appointment only.\r\nFeatures\r\nLarge three bedroom property\r\nSouth facing garden\r\nOff street parking\r\nDouble Glazed\r\nO.F.C.H.\r\nPrime location\r\nClose to a host of local amenities"
      },
      {
